{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"596","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Wilbur and Array"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wilbur the pig is tinkering with arrays again. He has the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" initially consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" zeros. At one step, he can choose any index "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" and either add "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to all elements "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai, ai + 1, ... , an"},{"kind":"text","text":" or subtract "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" from all elements "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai, ai + 1, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":". His goal is to end up with the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b1, b2, ..., bn"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Of course, Wilbur wants to achieve this goal in the minimum number of steps and asks you to compute this value."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 200 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". Initially "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" for every position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":", so this array is not given in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of the input contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b1, b2, ..., bn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 109 ≤ bi ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the minimum number of steps that Wilbur needs to make in order to achieve "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai = bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" for all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1 2 3 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n1 2 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, Wilbur may successively choose indices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":", and add "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to corresponding suffixes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, Wilbur first chooses indices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and adds "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to corresponding suffixes, then he chooses index "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and subtract "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"596B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/596/problem/B"}